WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:03.467
-We're talking about romantic comedies tonight. It's great.

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:04.634
-It's a real rom-com kind of night!

00:00:04.634 --> 00:00:05.901
-I love that. -I like it.

00:00:05.901 --> 00:00:07.834
-I love a romantic comedy. But do you --

00:00:07.834 --> 00:00:09.601
When you're writing this, do you go,

00:00:09.601 --> 00:00:11.734
"Oh, something like this kind of happened in my life.

00:00:11.734 --> 00:00:14.167
I'll put this into the movie"? -A little bit.

00:00:14.167 --> 00:00:17.267
I mean, you know, the main premise of the movie

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:18.801
is not about us, luckily,

00:00:18.801 --> 00:00:21.801
but we put a lot of little details into it, for sure.

00:00:21.801 --> 00:00:24.067
And, like, Dave's a romantic guy,

00:00:24.067 --> 00:00:27.734
so we certainly had some situations early on,

00:00:27.734 --> 00:00:29.334
you know, when we first started dating.

00:00:29.334 --> 00:00:31.734
We spent the first, like, six weeks of our relationship

00:00:31.734 --> 00:00:32.934
in different cities.

00:00:32.934 --> 00:00:34.868
He was shooting a movie called "Now You See Me."

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:36.534
And so we met -- [ Audience oohs ]

00:00:36.534 --> 00:00:40.467
Alright! Some magic fans in the audience.

00:00:40.467 --> 00:00:42.234
So, we met in New Orleans during Mardi Gras

00:00:42.234 --> 00:00:44.934
when he was shooting that. And then the movie took him to New York,

00:00:44.934 --> 00:00:46.534
and we kind of re-met up in New York.

00:00:46.534 --> 00:00:48.100
And he was going to finish shooting the movie in Paris.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:50.434
So, while we're in New York, he hides a little --

00:00:50.434 --> 00:00:54.534
My last day in New York, he hides a little note in my shoe.

00:00:54.534 --> 00:00:56.968
And when I'm putting my shoe on, I get this little note.

00:00:56.968 --> 00:00:59.100
And it says, "Meet me in Paris."

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:00.734
And there's a little drawing

00:01:00.734 --> 00:01:02.868
of two stick figures and the Eiffel Tower.

00:01:02.868 --> 00:01:04.667
-What? -So then I'm going to go

00:01:04.667 --> 00:01:06.267
to Paris and I tell my friends,

00:01:06.267 --> 00:01:07.667
"I'm meeting this new guy I'm seeing in Paris."

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:09.167
And they're like, "You've got to go to this bridge,

00:01:09.167 --> 00:01:10.667
the Pont des Arts.

00:01:10.667 --> 00:01:13.667
People put their initials on locks

00:01:13.667 --> 00:01:15.200
and they lock it on the bridge,

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:17.000
and it means they're going to be together forever.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:19.033
And they throw the keys into the Seine!"

00:01:19.033 --> 00:01:20.200
-yeah. -I was like --

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:21.601
-Throw the key.

00:01:21.601 --> 00:01:23.701
-"Slow your roll. I just met this guy."

00:01:23.701 --> 00:01:25.701
-Yeah, I'm not locking my love with this guy.

00:01:25.701 --> 00:01:27.901
-Yeah. Also, like, I don't need to put that message out to him.

00:01:27.901 --> 00:01:30.634
Like, let me try to be cool and aloof a little bit.

00:01:30.634 --> 00:01:33.734
-Yeah, smart. -So, we get to Paris.

00:01:33.734 --> 00:01:36.634
We're walking around one day. It's raining.

00:01:36.634 --> 00:01:39.367
Dave gives me his jacket. So sweet.

00:01:39.367 --> 00:01:42.000
-Yeah. -I put my hand in the pocket

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:46.968
and pull out a little lock that has our initials on it.

00:01:46.968 --> 00:01:48.667
And I looked at him and was like,

00:01:48.667 --> 00:01:52.868
"[ Gasps ] You like me! Oh, my God!"

00:01:52.868 --> 00:01:55.067
-Here's -- Here's the -- -We locked it on the bridge.

00:01:55.067 --> 00:01:56.267
-Here it is.

00:01:56.267 --> 00:01:58.334
-And we've been together ever since.

00:01:58.334 --> 00:02:00.200
[ Cheers and applause ] -Are you kidding me?

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:02.801
That's the most romantic thing in the world.

00:02:02.801 --> 00:02:06.100
-I mean, he's in love with me. -I love that.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:09.267
Do -- Do you go -- Have you ever been back to visit the bridge?

00:02:09.267 --> 00:02:13.033
-We did go back, and I guess the locks

00:02:13.033 --> 00:02:17.133
were, like, sagging down the whole bridge

00:02:17.133 --> 00:02:21.000
and compromising its inherent nature as a bridge

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:24.133
and they cut -- they cut all the locks off.

00:02:24.133 --> 00:02:25.601
They put up big fencing

00:02:25.601 --> 00:02:27.834
so nobody can put a lock on ever again.

00:02:27.834 --> 00:02:29.067
-Oh, my God. Are you kidding me?

00:02:29.067 --> 00:02:31.167
-Yeah, so I guess we're going to get divorced.

00:02:31.167 --> 00:02:32.300
-No, that's not what it meant. No.

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:34.267
That -- No. This love is here to stay.

00:02:34.267 --> 00:02:35.868
-We have to. We have the photo. We have the photo.

00:02:35.868 --> 00:02:37.367
-You have the photo. Yeah. Love lives forever.

00:02:37.367 --> 00:02:40.267
-Okay. Yes, yes! [ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:40.267 --> 00:02:42.968
-Let's -- I want to talk about the movie and -- and the plot

00:02:42.968 --> 00:02:45.067
of the movie "Somebody I Used to Know."

00:02:45.067 --> 00:02:47.734
-Yes. -But since you're always

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:50.067
down for a game and something fun on our show,

00:02:50.067 --> 00:02:51.734
I thought it would be fun if you

00:02:51.734 --> 00:02:54.534
would like to freestyle a rap what the movie is about.

00:02:54.534 --> 00:02:56.434
-You've done this to me before.

00:02:56.434 --> 00:02:57.701
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.701 --> 00:02:59.234
-It makes me -- -You've done this to me before.

00:02:59.234 --> 00:03:00.767
-It makes me laugh. It makes me laugh.

00:03:00.767 --> 00:03:03.701
It -- But, I mean. Here's wh-- You're not a rapper.

00:03:03.701 --> 00:03:05.968
-Look, I'm not a rapper.

00:03:05.968 --> 00:03:08.100
So let's just say that before we do anything else.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:10.133
-'Cause everyone thought that when you came out.

00:03:10.133 --> 00:03:11.534
Everyone's like, "Oh, Alison Brie, the rapper."

00:03:11.534 --> 00:03:14.133
-The rapper. I know. I'm known in certain circles.

00:03:14.133 --> 00:03:17.534
But just to dispel that rumor -- -So you are not a rapper.

00:03:17.534 --> 00:03:20.033
But would you like to -- -I will do the honors tonight.

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:21.701
-Wow. -If you guys wanna --

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:23.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:23.701 --> 00:03:25.167
Quest will drop a beat.

00:03:25.167 --> 00:03:26.234
♪♪

00:03:26.234 --> 00:03:29.934
Oh. Alright. I'm feeling it. Okay.

00:03:29.934 --> 00:03:32.868
And we're about to go in 3, 2, 1.

00:03:32.868 --> 00:03:34.534
